    <section id="vision" class="vision section-shell">
      <div class="vision-intro"><p class="eyebrow">Why the Philippines?</p><h2>A great need.<br />A willing family.</h2><p>In the summers of 2024 and 2025, our family visited the Philippines. During those trips, I had opportunities to share the Gospel with old friends and acquaintances, factory workers, police officers, hospital workers, and many others. I witnessed God working in hearts and saw a genuine hunger among Filipinos for the truth of His Word. God used these experiences to open my eyes to the great need for laborers and renewed my desire to serve Him full-time.</p><p>The Philippines is home to more than 117 million people. It is a deeply religious nation, yet many are deeply rooted in a false gospel of works-based salvation rather than faith in Jesus Christ alone.</p><p>According to the 2020 Census, 78.8 percent identified as Roman Catholic, 6.4 percent as Muslim, 4.8% as Evangelical, and 2.6% as Iglesia ni Cristo, while Bible Baptist Church accounted for only 0.5%. There are millions of people who still need to hear the Gospel.</p><p>God has used faithful American missionaries and raised up many Filipino Baptist preachers and missionaries. We believe there remains a tremendous need for independent, fundamental Baptist churches that faithfully proclaim the Gospel, stand firmly on the authority of Scripture, actively engage in soul winning, and carry out the Great Commission.</p></div>
